Step 1: Create a GCP Project
Create a new Google Cloud project.
Project Name: Spiritual Portal
Step 2: Enable Required APIs
Enable the Compute Engine API.
Verify that the API is enabled before creating Compute Engine resources.
Step 3: Create a VPC Network
Go to VPC Network → Create VPC Network
Provide:
VPC Name: prod-vpc1
Choose one of the following subnet modes:
Option 1: Custom Mode
Create your own subnet.
Example:
Subnet Name: app-subnet
Region: asia-south1
IP Stack Type: IPv4 (or IPv4/IPv6 if required)
CIDR Range: e.g., 10.10.0.0/24
Option 2: Automatic Mode
Google automatically creates subnets in all regions.
Step 4: Create Cloud NAT
Go to:
Network Services → Cloud NAT
Create a new Cloud NAT and configure:
NAT Gateway Name
Region
VPC Network
Cloud Router
Purpose:
Cloud NAT allows private VM instances (without external IPs) to access the internet for software updates and package downloads.
Step 5: Configure Firewall Rules
Go to:
VPC Network → Firewall
Create firewall rules such as:
Health Check Rule
Allow Google's health check IP ranges.
Used by Load Balancer.
Proxy Rule
Allow traffic from Load Balancer proxies to backend instances.
Common interview ports:
SSH → Port 22
HTTP → Port 80
HTTPS → Port 443
Step 6: Create an Instance Template
Configure:
Instance Template Name
Region
Machine Type
Example:
e2-micro
2 vCPU
1 GB Memory
Configure:
VPC Network
Subnet
Service Account
Firewall Tags
Startup Script:
#!/bin/bash
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable --now flask.service
The startup script automatically starts the Flask application whenever a VM is created from the template.
Step 7: Create a Managed Instance Group (MIG)
Create a Managed Instance Group using the Instance Template.
Configure:
Group Name
Region
Instance Template
Minimum Number of Instances
Autoscaling (Optional)
Purpose:
Automatically creates VM instances.
Recreates unhealthy instances.
Supports Auto Scaling.
Integrates with Load Balancer.
